            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="TAY15" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>'Opera'</forename>
                        <surname>Taylor</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>singer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Identification uncertain. In <title>The London Stage 1776-1800</title>, Beecher Hogan lists a 
    Taylor who makes his first appearance on the stage on 20 April 1798, Covent Garden. He played the lead
  in the afterpiece <title>The Waterman</title> where he sang 'Old England's Tree of Liberty'. Hogan notes that he previously sang at Vauxhall which is where he 
    may have gained the soubriquet 'Opera Taylor'.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Charles Beecher Hogan, <title>The London Stage 1776-1800</title> (Carbondale: Southern Illinois University Press, 1968).</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
